# 16. CENTRAL DATABASE ARCHITECTURE

This is the most important part of NEXUS OS.

Use Firebase Firestore as the Single Source of Truth.

All modules must read and update shared database records.

### Suggested Firestore Collections

```text
users/
  userId

projects/
  projectId

tasks/
  taskId

routines/
  routineId

routineCompletions/
  completionId

calendarEvents/
  eventId

raciAssignments/
  assignmentId

focusSessions/
  sessionId

vocabulary/
  wordId

transactions/
  transactionId

budgets/
  budgetId

notifications/
  notificationId

activityLogs/
  logId

integrations/
  integrationId

syncLogs/
  syncId
```

You may improve this structure when necessary, but maintain clear relationships and avoid unnecessary data duplication.

### Important Data Relationships

**Project → Tasks**

One project can contain multiple tasks.

**Task → RACI**

Each task can have responsibility assignments.

**Task → Calendar**

Tasks with deadlines or scheduled dates can be represented in the calendar.

**Task → Gantt**

The Gantt Chart must use the original Task records.

**Task → KPI**

Performance metrics must calculate from actual task records.

**Routine → Completion History**

Routine completion must maintain historical records.

**Focus Session → Task**

A focus session can optionally be associated with a task.

**Transaction → Account Type**

Each transaction must belong to either Personal or Business.

Use stable unique IDs and timestamps.

Include:
- createdAt.
- updatedAt.
- createdBy.
- updatedBy.
- archivedAt where applicable.

# 17. UNIFIED DATA SYNCHRONIZATION ENGINE

Implement a centralized synchronization architecture.

### Single Source of Truth

Firestore is the primary database.

The following modules must use shared records:

- Dashboard.
- Task Manager.
- To-Do List.
- Calendar.
- Routine Planner.
- RACI Matrix.
- KPI & Metrics.
- Gantt Chart.

### Synchronization Rules

| Action | Required Updates |
|---|---|
| Create Task | Kanban, To-Do, Gantt, Dashboard |
| Change Deadline | Calendar, Gantt, Task Manager |
| Change Status | Kanban, KPI, Dashboard |
| Change Assigned Person | RACI, Gantt, Workload |
| Complete Task | KPI, Dashboard, Kanban |
| Update Routine | Routine Planner, Calendar |
| Delete Task | All related views |
| Update Project | Project Overview, Gantt |

### Two Types of Updates

**Unified Update**

Changes made in one module automatically reflect in all related modules.

**Individual Update**

Users can edit information from any relevant module.

All updates must modify the same central record instead of creating separate copies.

### Synchronization Reliability

Implement:

- Real-Time Updates.
- Conflict Management.
- Duplicate Prevention.
- Sync History.
- Retry Mechanism.
- Error Logging.
- Undo / Recovery.
- Soft Delete Synchronization.

For external integrations, use stable external IDs and idempotent synchronization operations.

Do not rely on frontend-only synchronization.

Use Firebase Cloud Functions or an appropriate secure backend service for external API synchronization.

Maintain a clear separation between internal database updates and external integration updates.

